.Dd $Mdocdate$
.Dt DISK-AGENT.YAML 5
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm disk-agent.yaml
.Nd configuration files for the Disk Agent
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The configuration of
.Xr disk-agent 8
is a directory of two YAML files:
.Pa app.config.yaml
and
.Pa auth.config.yaml .
Each carries
.Cm schemaVersion
and the sections listed below that belong to it; a key absent from a file
takes the default its schema declares.
.Pp
Location:
.Pa /etc/disk-agent/
(seeded by the package, passed via
.Fl -config
or
.Ev CONFIG_DIR ) .
.Sh CONFIGURATION SECTIONS
.Ss server
HTTP/HTTPS server configuration.
.Bl -tag -width "bind_address"
.It Cm bind_address
IP address to bind the web server to (default: "0.0.0.0")
.It Cm port
TCP port number for the HTTP server (default: 9430)
.It Cm https_port
TCP port number for the HTTPS listener, bound only when
.Cm ssl.enabled
(default: 9431)
.El
.Ss ssl
HTTPS/TLS configuration. Certificate problems never stop the agent; HTTPS
is skipped with an error in the log and HTTP keeps serving.
.Bl -tag -width "generate_ssl"
.It Cm enabled
Boolean serving HTTPS on
.Cm server.https_port
(default: true). With SSL up, the plain-HTTP port serves only redirects to
HTTPS unless
.Cm force_secure
is false.
.It Cm force_secure
Boolean making the plain-HTTP port serve only 308 redirects to HTTPS while
the TLS listener is up (default: true).
.It Cm generate_ssl
Boolean generating the server certificate at the paths below when none
exists, signed by the CA at the CA paths, the CA itself generated when
absent (default: true)
.It Cm key_path
Server TLS private key location. Empty uses
.Pa ssl/server.key
beside the configuration files (default: empty).
.It Cm cert_path
Server TLS certificate location. Empty uses
.Pa ssl/server.crt
beside the configuration files (default: empty).
.It Cm ca_cert_path
CA certificate that signs the generated server certificate. Empty uses
.Pa <config dir>/ssl/ca.crt .
.It Cm ca_key_path
CA private key location (PKCS#1, PKCS#8, or EC). Empty uses
.Pa <config dir>/ssl/ca.key .
.El
.Ss cors
Cross-Origin Resource Sharing. The API key, not the browser Origin, is the
access boundary.
.Bl -tag -width "allow_all"
.It Cm allow_all
Boolean answering any browser Origin (default: true)
.It Cm whitelist
List of origins (scheme://host:port) allowed when
.Cm allow_all
is false (default: empty)
.El
.Ss logging
Logging configuration.
.Bl -tag -width "max_size_mb"
.It Cm level
Logging level: "error", "warn", "info", or "debug" (default: "info")
.It Cm console
Boolean enabling human-readable logging on standard error (default: true)
.It Cm file
Log file path. Empty uses
.Pa logs/agent.log
beside the configuration files (default: empty).
.It Cm max_size_mb
Maximum log file size in megabytes before rotation (default: 20)
.It Cm max_backups
Number of rotated log files to keep (default: 5)
.It Cm compression
Boolean gzip-compressing rotated log files (default: true)
.It Cm categories
Map of per-category log levels overriding the global level. Categories the
agent emits: app, api_requests, auth (default: empty)
.El
.Ss collection
The tools the collector runs on every GET /api/report.
.Bl -tag -width "privilege_command"
.It Cm smartctl_path
The smartctl binary; a bare name is looked up on PATH (default: "smartctl";
the Debian package seeds /usr/sbin/smartctl, the OmniOS package
/opt/ooce/sbin/smartctl)
.It Cm zpool_path
The zpool binary (default: "zpool"; the Debian package seeds /sbin/zpool,
the OmniOS package /usr/sbin/zpool)
.It Cm privilege_command
Prepended to every smartctl and zpool call: sudo on Debian, pfexec on
OmniOS; empty runs them as the service user (default: empty; each package
seeds its own)
.El
.Ss api_keys
API-key authentication.
.Bl -tag -width "bootstrap_require_claim_token"
.It Cm bootstrap_enabled
Boolean enabling POST /api/api-keys/bootstrap to create the first API key
(default: true)
.It Cm bootstrap_auto_disable
Boolean locking the bootstrap endpoint once any key exists (default: true)
.It Cm bootstrap_require_claim_token
Boolean requiring the setup (claim) token, written to
.Pa setup.token
beside the configuration files and printed to the startup log, as proof of
host ownership (default: true)
.It Cm hash_rounds
Bcrypt cost for stored key hashes, 4-20 (default: 12)
.It Cm key_length
Random bytes of key material, 16-256, base64url-encoded after the da_
prefix (default: 64)
.El
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width ".Pa /etc/disk-agent/<name>.config.yaml"
.It Pa /etc/disk-agent/<name>.config.yaml
Configuration files (app, auth)
.It Pa /usr/share/disk-agent/config/<name>.config.yaml
The seed files the Debian package installs and postinst copies into place
.It Pa /var/log/disk-agent/
Service log directory
.It Pa /var/lib/disk-agent/
Service data directory
.El
.Pp
Beside the configuration files the agent also keeps
.Pa setup.token
(first-key claim token, 0600),
.Pa keys.json
(hashed API keys, 0600), and
.Pa backups/
(configuration backups).
.Sh EXAMPLES
The packaged default: two files under
.Pa /etc/disk-agent ,
each containing only:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
schemaVersion: 1
.Ed
.Pp
Every key absent from a file takes the default its schema declares.
.Sh DIAGNOSTICS
Configuration errors prevent the agent from starting and are reported on
standard error and in the journal:
.Pp
.Dl # journalctl -u disk-agent
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr disk-agent 8 ,
.Xr systemctl 1 ,
.Xr journalctl 1
.Sh STANDARDS
The configuration files use YAML 1.2 format as defined by the YAML
specification; each file's schema is JSON Schema 2020-12, served at
GET /api/config/<name>/schema.
